WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.430
Scarlet Witch is a fairly new addition to
the Marvel Cinematic Universe, although she

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:09.240
has a rich and bizarre comic history that
goes as far back as most of the Avengers.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.120
When it comes to getting her own standalone
movie, that lengthy history might actually

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.849
hurt more than it helps.

00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:18.680
Here's why we think Marvel won't give Scarlet
Witch her own movie.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.880
Olsen’s not sold

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.130
Elizabeth Olsen, the actress who plays Scarlet
Witch, has been enjoying a nice career lift

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:28.520
from the MCU, but isn’t sold on doing a
solo movie.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:34.079
She said: "The pressure of a tentpole movie
on my shoulders doesn't feel comfortable."

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:37.660
In the meantime, she's taken advantage of
the tight scheduling of the Marvel machine

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:38.780
to find other projects.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.840
Though she’s obviously hesitant, Olsen did
admit she might be interested, though the

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.670
story would "have to make sense for how it
advances the world."

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:47.670
Toy troubles

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.960
Times are changing, but not that quickly.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:55.659
Captain America: Civil War has the distinction
of having the most female heroes of all the

00:00:55.659 --> 00:00:58.910
MCU movies so far — and that’s definitely
a good thing.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:03.089
However, just like Black Widow in the previous
Avengers films, Scarlet Witch figures were

00:01:03.089 --> 00:01:06.830
scarce to practically non-existent in the
movie's initial toy line.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:09.150
Take this Avengers vs. Ultron box set.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.330
It's got nine figures — nine!

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:15.760
And while it doesn't include Black Widow or
Scarlet Witch, two of the film's most important

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.430
characters, it does manage to find room for
a figure called..."Sub-Ultron?"

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:21.540
Yikes.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:25.390
Marvel has been working on these diversity
oversights, and both Scarlet Witch and Black

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:29.470
Widow eventually got their own action figures
— multiple versions, in fact — but the

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:34.100
historic reluctance to lean heavily on its
female heroes doesn't bode well for the possibilities

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:37.290
of Scarlet Witch being allowed to carry a
standalone film.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:40.950
Like it or not, toys are still big business
when it comes to superhero movies.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:46.020
If they don’t think a Scarlet Witch toy
will sell, it makes a movie even less likely.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.010
Bonkers backstory

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:51.080
Scarlet Witch is a great character for an
ensemble cast.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:55.170
She has a cool look, cool powers, and her
magic skills are a nice balance to heroes

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.240
with tech weapons and hand-to-hand skills.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.710
But, as useful as that might be, there are
a whole lot of problems once you dig a bit

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:02.710
deeper.

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:06.990
Wanda Maximoff’s history goes back to the
same Silver Age comics era as the Avengers,

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:10.590
with her first appearance coming only a year
after the team's debut.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:15.290
Most comic book storylines got pretty weird
in the 1960s, but hers set the gold standard

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:16.290
for wacky.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:20.160
Wanda and her brother Pietro, better known
as Quicksilver, were born after their mother

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:25.090
fled their father — more on him later — and
were adopted by a guy called the High Evolutionary.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:28.180
Oh, and they were also raised by a cow.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.530
Yes, an actual cow.

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:30.939
Her name is Bova!

00:02:30.939 --> 00:02:33.870
And that's actually only the start of Scarlet
Witch's weirdness.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:37.590
Her powers powers are basically magic, and
in both the movies and comics, she gained

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.379
them by being experimented on.

00:02:39.379 --> 00:02:43.190
Looking back to the comics, most of Scarlet
Witch's powers are actually channeled through

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:45.099
a demon god named Chthon.

00:02:45.099 --> 00:02:49.060
But she's also gained additional powers through
deals with the character Mephisto — who

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.719
is basically Marvel’s version of the devil.

00:02:51.719 --> 00:02:55.859
Between her having a cow for a mom and all
the business she does with literal demons,

00:02:55.859 --> 00:03:04.050
making a movie that's true to her comics roots
might be, well, a little challenging.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.150
Family film issues

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:11.080
The cinematic rights to Marvel's X-Men franchise
have been owned by Fox for a long while.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:15.200
With the Marvel Cinematic Universe owned by
Disney, the odds for a crossover are pretty

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.500
much nonexistent.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.200
So things can get a little touchy when you
have characters related to one another spread

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.680
between the two companies.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.709
For decades of comic book history, it was
pretty clearly established that Magneto is

00:03:25.709 --> 00:03:28.709
Scarlet Witch and Quicksilver’s biological
father.

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:32.889
Meanwhile, Marvel has since made that point
a bit looser with some recent storylines that

00:03:32.889 --> 00:03:37.019
suggest the twins were never mutants in the
first place — possibly in an effort to better

00:03:37.019 --> 00:03:38.019
match the films.

00:03:38.019 --> 00:03:42.439
But no matter how you slice it, Scarlet Witch
and Magneto have tons of comic book history

00:03:42.439 --> 00:03:43.439
together.

00:03:43.439 --> 00:03:47.689
For a movie to push all that out of the way
could potentially alienate longtime fans.

00:03:47.689 --> 00:03:49.239
Too powerful?

00:03:49.239 --> 00:03:53.749
One of the toughest challenges in writing
a character like Scarlet Witch is that they

00:03:53.749 --> 00:03:56.730
haven’t actually established an upper limit
to her powers.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:00.889
At various times in the comics she's re-written
time and shifted reality, resurrected the

00:04:00.889 --> 00:04:03.730
dead and brought characters to life out of
thin air.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:07.559
At one point, she willed the entire mutant
species out of existence.

00:04:07.559 --> 00:04:11.360
In the same way screenwriters often struggle
to come up with worthwhile challenges for

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:15.749
characters like Superman and Hulk, Scarlet
Witch could pose a similar problem.

00:04:15.749 --> 00:04:20.400
It's one thing to have her save the day for
a few moments at a time in an ensemble picture.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:21.400
But on her own?

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.620
Whipping up a movie like that might be the
one power she doesn't have.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:25.960
Thanks for watching!

